<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Raise Horde</h1>
<p>Sphere: Creation Sphere
Class: Necromancer (guild level 150)
Mana: 20, and 10 for each corpse
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast raise horde
tell horde &lt;command&gt;
</pre>
<p>The necromancer cuts themself, bleeds upon the ground and chants 
'Multitudenem aneme', and every corpse in the room rises at once: about 
four in ten as skeletons, four in ten as zombies, and the rest as skeletal 
champions. Each follows its maker and carries what the corpse held.
</p><p>You need at least 100 mana to begin, and each corpse raised costs you 10 
more; when your mana runs low, the raising stops. Corpses of insects and 
other crawling things, of the undead, demons and devils, elementals, 
golems, gargoyles and the like crumble to dust instead.
</p><p>Command your horde with tell, just as with <a cmd='#'>Help Animate Dead</a>: tell horde 
kill rat. The undead last a few minutes, up to a quarter of an hour or 
more for a master, then crumble to dust, leaving what they carried. A 
strong dispel magic ends them sooner. They never attack players, unless 
both you and they have signed the Book of Blood.
</p><p>You must be standing, and no free hands are needed. It is also found on 
wands, staffs and scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
